#
# Configuration for the virtual network device sample.
#
# The virtual Ethernet link itself is now provided by the in-tree
# "zephyr,ipc-ethernet" driver (CONFIG_ETH_IPC), instantiated from the
# vnet0 devicetree node in each board overlay. The options below only
# configure the sample's UDP demo application on top of that link.

config VNET
	bool "Virtual network device UDP demo"
	default y
	select NETWORKING
	select NET_L2_ETHERNET
	help
	  Build the UDP demo application that runs the network stack over the
	  vnet0 interface provided by the zephyr,ipc-ethernet driver. Frames
	  cross between the two cores through a shared-memory ring signalled by
	  an MBOX doorbell.

if VNET

config VNET_DEMO_PEER_ADDR
	string "Peer IPv4 address(es) the demo sends UDP datagrams to"
	default "192.0.2.1,192.0.2.10"
	help
	  The demo TX loop sends to this address on every cycle. This may be a
	  comma-separated list (up to 4 addresses) to send to several peers at
	  once. By default the host targets the remote core (192.0.2.1) and a
	  PC (192.0.2.10), and the remote targets the host core (192.0.2.2) and
	  the PC (192.0.2.10). The PC is reachable through the host's
	  vnet0<->Ethernet bridge (see VNET_BRIDGE).

config VNET_BRIDGE
	bool "Bridge vnet0 with the real Ethernet interface (host only)"
	select NET_ETHERNET_BRIDGE
	help
	  On the host core, transparently L2-bridge the virtual interface
	  (vnet0) with the on-board Ethernet interface. This lets the remote
	  core reach an off-chip host (e.g. a PC on the same subnet) via the
	  shared-memory link and the host's Ethernet port. When enabled, the
	  host acts as a bridge rather than running the UDP demo itself.

endif # VNET
